        "title": "Trees and Forests - Structure, Succession, and Old Growth",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "A forest is not a collection of trees — it is a self-organizing, multi-trophic ecosystem with physical structure that spans vertical space from canopy to forest floor. The emergent properties of a mature forest (microclimate buffering, carbon storage, water regulation, biodiversity) cannot be recovered for centuries after disturbance. Understanding forests requires understanding both individual tree biology and ecosystem-level dynamics."
    },
