      "text": "### Primary Succession (bare rock → forest)"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-TREES-FORESTS.md#015",
      "path": [
        "06-TREES-FORESTS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[proof-backfill:botany:06-trees-forests, git-history:botany:06-trees-forests]",
        "canonical_path": "botany/06-TREES-FORESTS.md",
        "concepts": "[trees, forests]",
        "current_path": "botany/06-TREES-FORESTS.md",
        "id": "maxim:botany:trees-forests",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "botany",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[trees, forests]",
        "section": "botany",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Trees and Forests - Structure, Succession, and Old Growth",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nPRIMARY SUCCESSION (approximately, temperate)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nBare rock/glacial scour/volcanic ash\n    │ lichen and mosses\n    │ weather rock to soil, accumulate organic matter\n    ▼ (decades)\nPioneer herbs and annuals\n    │ fireweed, annual grasses, nitrogen-fixing herbs\n    │ begin soil building\n    ▼ (5-20 years)\nPerennial grasses and forbs\n    │ taller vegetation shades out pioneers\n    ▼ (10-30 years)\nShrubs\n    │ willow, alder, shrubby cinquefoil\n    │ alder: nitrogen-fixing → accelerates succession\n    ▼ (20-50 years)\nPioneer trees\n    │ birch, aspen, poplar, pine → fast-growing, sun-demanding\n    │ create shade below them → enable next stage\n    ▼ (50-100 years)\nShade-tolerant trees begin\n    │ (maple, beech, hemlock, spruce depending on region)\n    │ grow in understory of pioneer trees\n    ▼ (50-200 years)\n\"Climax\" / late-successional forest\n    │ steady state (not static — disturbance creates internal dynamics)\n```"
    },
