        "title": "Trees and Forests - Structure, Succession, and Old Growth",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\nSECONDARY SUCCESSION (abandoned farm → forest, ~150 years)\n──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────\nYear 1-3:     Annual weeds (crabgrass, ragweed, goldenrod)\nYear 3-10:    Perennial grasses + shrubs (blackberry, elderberry)\nYear 10-25:   Pioneer trees (gray birch, aspen, pin cherry, eastern red cedar)\nYear 25-75:   Early-successional forest (young canopy, dense)\nYear 75-150:  Mid-successional forest\nYear 150+:    Late-successional (depending on region, climate, disturbance)\n```"
    },
