      },
      "text": "**The \"climax community\" concept:** F.E. Clements (~1920) proposed that succession ends in a single stable \"climax\" community determined by climate. Now known to be wrong — forests are not in equilibrium; disturbance (fire, wind, disease, drought) continually resets patches. The landscape is a mosaic of different successional stages."
    },
